1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:03,299
Contacts gives your department a shared
directory of people,

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,309
organizations, and locations.

3
00:00:05,679 --> 00:00:09,960
Keep member accounts and roster roles in
Personnel; use this directory

4
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,119
for useful operational references.

5
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,630
In our fictional Chicago Fire training
department, we are in

6
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:17,770
Contacts, on the Categories page.

7
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:22,979
The category table separates its name,
description, color, and contact count.

8
00:00:23,299 --> 00:00:26,110
It starts empty here, even though the
department already

9
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:28,069
has uncategorized contacts.

10
00:00:28,379 --> 00:00:32,380
We will create a small partner directory
and verify each saved entry.

11
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,089
Choose Add Category.

12
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:38,949
Enter Academy Partner Directory as the
Name and describe it as fictional

13
00:00:38,949 --> 00:00:41,330
training partners and logistics contacts.

14
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:44,849
Keep the blue color so the category is
easy to recognize.

15
00:00:45,179 --> 00:00:49,369
Display On Map remains unchecked and Map
Icon stays Default.

16
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,469
Those controls are separate from
organizing the directory.

17
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:55,560
Save, then read the returned category row.

18
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,310
Its name, description, and blue color are
present, while

19
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:01,439
Contacts In Category is zero.

20
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:04,879
That saved row is our starting point for
adding contacts.

21
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:10,139
On the Add Contact form, select Person,
then Academy Partner Directory.

22
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:13,880
Enter Sylvie and Brett in the first and
last name fields.

23
00:01:14,249 --> 00:01:18,520
The organization field can add context;
here it contains Academy

24
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,670
Community Partners, marked fictional.

25
00:01:21,119 --> 00:01:24,900
Email Address and Cell Phone hold
deliberately reserved training values.

26
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,349
Scroll to Description and explain the
purpose of the entry.

27
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,529
Our text identifies a fictional community
partner liaison and

28
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:36,560
asks the reader to verify current details
before operational use.

29
00:01:36,929 --> 00:01:39,450
Keep that description useful and specific.

30
00:01:39,629 --> 00:01:44,119
After saving the person, use the Contacts
table Search field to enter Brett.

31
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:48,950
The result shows Sylvie Brett, the Person
type, and the named category.

32
00:01:49,259 --> 00:01:53,049
Choose View and check the saved name and
training contact channels.

33
00:01:53,389 --> 00:01:55,870
Scroll down to read the complete
Description again.

34
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:59,290
These separate checks confirm that both
the identity and the

35
00:01:59,290 --> 00:02:00,829
useful context were stored.

36
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:05,419
To verify category membership, use the
named category in the list or

37
00:02:05,419 --> 00:02:09,989
the edit form; the Additional Info
category value on this View is numeric.

38
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:13,230
Create a second entry using Location or
Company.

39
00:02:13,659 --> 00:02:17,819
Keep the same category, leave the person
name fields empty, and enter

40
00:02:17,849 --> 00:02:22,229
Academy Logistics Desk, marked fictional,
in Company Location Name.

41
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:27,059
The organization has its own reserved
training email and an Office Phone

42
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:29,030
ending in zero one four three.

43
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:32,690
Its Description explains that it is a
fictional supply and

44
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:34,620
mutual-aid coordination contact.

45
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:38,120
Using the appropriate contact type and
phone field makes the

46
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:41,680
directory easier to understand when
someone else opens the entry.

47
00:02:41,910 --> 00:02:47,209
In Location Info, GPS Location has a
latitude field and a longitude field.

48
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,499
Enter the complete fictional Chicago pair
together.

49
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:55,560
Entrance GPS Location and Exit GPS
Location are separate pairs

50
00:02:55,610 --> 00:02:57,430
and stay blank in this exercise.

51
00:02:57,899 --> 00:03:01,919
Continue to Physical Address and enter the
fictional Training Avenue street,

52
00:03:02,069 --> 00:03:04,159
Chicago, Illinois, and postal code.

53
00:03:04,639 --> 00:03:08,610
Check Same as Physical under Mailing
Address, then use Save

54
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,799
at the bottom of the form.

55
00:03:10,309 --> 00:03:14,520
These are stored directory reference
values; entering coordinates does not

56
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:18,920
establish a device position, a verified
entrance, or a successful route.

57
00:03:19,110 --> 00:03:23,570
Back in Contacts, select Academy Partner
Directory in the category tree.

58
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:28,890
Both newly saved entries appear: the
person and the logistics organization.

59
00:03:29,359 --> 00:03:31,489
Now enter Logistics in Search.

60
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:36,410
The table narrows the selected category to
the organization, and the count says that

61
00:03:36,410 --> 00:03:38,919
one result is filtered from two entries.

62
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:42,380
Read the name and type before choosing
View or Edit.

63
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:47,019
A short list can reflect the combination
of these filters, so check the selected

64
00:03:47,019 --> 00:03:50,749
category and search text before deciding
that an entry is missing.

65
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:52,539
Open the saved organization.

66
00:03:53,030 --> 00:03:56,910
Contact Details shows its name and email,
and Location Info

67
00:03:56,910 --> 00:03:58,689
shows the stored coordinate pair.

68
00:03:59,090 --> 00:04:02,980
Farther down, verify the physical address
and original Description.

69
00:04:03,510 --> 00:04:06,800
For the named category and copied mailing
address, return

70
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,490
to the list and choose Edit.

71
00:04:08,929 --> 00:04:13,580
The category is selected by name, and the
reopened mailing fields contain the copied

72
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:16,269
street, city, state, and postal code.

73
00:04:16,730 --> 00:04:19,359
Same as Physical is clear on reopening
here.

74
00:04:19,769 --> 00:04:23,710
Check those actual fields rather than
assuming the blank mailing section on

75
00:04:23,710 --> 00:04:25,749
View proves that nothing was saved.

76
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:29,720
Use a small, easy-to-check edit to confirm
your maintenance workflow.

77
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:35,220
In the reopened organization form, Office
Phone ends in zero one four three.

78
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:37,550
Change that final digit to four.

79
00:04:37,949 --> 00:04:41,419
After saving and reopening the same
contact, the field now

80
00:04:41,449 --> 00:04:43,389
ends in zero one four four.

81
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:47,040
Read the reopened value, not just the
value you typed.

82
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:50,880
The original supply and mutual-aid
Description remains in place.

83
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:54,960
A successful change to one field is a
reason to verify that field

84
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:58,670
specifically, rather than assume every
attempted edit was stored.

85
00:04:58,950 --> 00:05:00,389
Finish in Categories.

86
00:05:00,809 --> 00:05:04,140
Academy Partner Directory now contains two
contacts.

87
00:05:04,539 --> 00:05:08,480
Give someone responsibility for reviewing
those details as partners change.

88
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:12,300
Chicago Fire can use this pattern for
logistics contacts.

89
00:05:12,659 --> 00:05:16,400
Community care and mental health teams can
maintain operational partner

90
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,410
directories without patient detail.

91
00:05:18,779 --> 00:05:23,330
Search and rescue can organize staging and
support contacts; security teams

92
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:27,759
can group site contacts; wildland crews
can maintain supply references;

93
00:05:28,009 --> 00:05:32,249
and industrial response teams can organize
facility coordination contacts.

94
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:36,830
In each setting, choose clear categories,
verify saved values,

95
00:05:37,089 --> 00:05:38,710
and keep the directory current.

